import{_ as t,o as i,c as n,a2 as o}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const c=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 384 | Dou Continent · Alaya Supervision Plan: Institutional Design to Prevent Soul-Beast Extinction","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 384 | Dou Continent · Alaya Supervision Plan: Institutional Design to Prevent Soul-Beast Extinction","no":384,"module":2,"tags":["Dou Continent","Alaya","Supervision","Soul-Beast Extinction","Institutional Design"],"related":["21-Symbiotic-Network Operating Principle","27-Anchor Calibration and Maintenance","46-Environmental Protection Law"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0384_模块2-斗罗-阿赖耶监管方案-杜绝魂兽灭绝的制度设计.md","filePath":"en/0384_模块2-斗罗-阿赖耶监管方案-杜绝魂兽灭绝的制度设计.md"}'),s={name:"en/0384_模块2-斗罗-阿赖耶监管方案-杜绝魂兽灭绝的制度设计.md"};function a(r,e,l,u,h,p){return i(),n("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[o('<h1 id="entry-384-dou-continent-·-alaya-supervision-plan-institutional-design-to-prevent-soul-beast-extinction" tabindex="-1">Entry 384 | Dou Continent · Alaya Supervision Plan: Institutional Design to Prevent Soul-Beast Extinction <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-384-dou-continent-·-alaya-supervision-plan-institutional-design-to-prevent-soul-beast-extinction" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 384 | Dou Continent · Alaya Supervision Plan: Institutional Design to Prevent Soul-Beast Extinction&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 2 · Myriad-Realms Benchmark Critique Library | Series: Dou Continent System Decomposition (Entry 25 · Institution) | Benchmark base: Documents 21, 27, 46</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-use-one-web-to-keep-watch-for-soul-beasts" tabindex="-1">Introduction: Use one web to keep watch for soul beasts <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-use-one-web-to-keep-watch-for-soul-beasts" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: Use one web to keep watch for soul beasts&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The root of soul-beast extinction in the Dou world is that no mechanism monitors populations or prevents over-hunting. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s answer is the Alaya Network — a supervision web covering the plane, mastering soul-beast population dynamics in real time, and auto-warning-and-intervening for red-line species. This entry, taking the law-first axiom as core, designs this supervision plan to prevent soul-beast extinction. Protagonist uniqueness dependency: <strong>Dou = high; after supervision = network-style</strong>. The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s judging base has been upgraded to the six top-level axioms.</p><h2 id="i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" tabindex="-1">I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Extinction is waste</strong>: every soul-beast species that goes extinct is irrecoverable loss</li><li><strong>Supervision gain</strong>: Alaya publicizes population data, avoiding blind action of &quot;not knowing it is endangered yet still hunting&quot;</li><li><strong>Warning stop-loss</strong>: red line triggers hunting stop, blocking waste before it happens</li></ul><h2 id="ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression-blocked-after-supervision" tabindex="-1">II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression (Blocked After Supervision) <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression-blocked-after-supervision" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression (Blocked After Supervision)&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Population sustainable</strong>: the supervision web matches catch volume with population regeneration capacity</li><li><strong>Red-line system</strong>: endangered species enter the red line; hunting institutionally forbidden</li><li><strong>Data-driven</strong>: no longer hunt by feel, but by data</li></ol><h2 id="iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking-after-supervision" tabindex="-1">III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking (After Supervision) <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking-after-supervision" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking (After Supervision)&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Hunting restricted</strong>: however strong a genius, hunting a red-line species is intercepted by the supervision web</li><li><strong>Interpretive right public</strong>: population data shared whole-network; no longer decided casually by strong ones &quot;how many remain&quot;</li><li><strong>Technology replacement first</strong>: the supervision web runs parallel with Path D, gradually reducing future hunting demand to zero</li></ul><h2 id="iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" tabindex="-1">IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Dou No Supervision</th><th>Alaya Supervision</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Blind hunting</td><td>Population data real-time public</td></tr><tr><td>Endangered no warning</td><td>Red line auto-warns</td></tr><tr><td>Strong ones can hunt anything</td><td>Red-line species unhuntable by all</td></tr><tr><td>Species silently extinct</td><td>Extinction blocked in advance</td></tr><tr><td>Data privately hoarded</td><td>Whole-network shared</td></tr></tbody></table><p>The alternative&#39;s crux: soul beasts&#39; safety relies not on strong ones&#39; kindness, but on a web no one can bypass.</p><p>The Alaya supervision web must be used in coordination with Path D · human-engineered Dao-Law soul rings: the supervision web guards today&#39;s soul-beast population red lines; Path D gradually reduces tomorrow&#39;s hunting demand to zero. Lin-Hao-style reconstructors grasp both hands — neither let existing soul beasts be hunted to extinction, nor let latecomers still have to hunt to level. Thus, &quot;hunted to extinction&quot; becomes institutionally impossible.</p><h2 id="v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" tabindex="-1">V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Modeling</strong>: replicate soul-beast population dynamics and supervision-web thresholds</li><li><strong>Variables</strong>: Group A no supervision; Group B Alaya supervision + Path D</li><li><strong>Observation</strong>: ten-thousand-year soul-beast population survival, species extinction rate</li><li><strong>Review</strong>: output &quot;Alaya Supervision Effectiveness Report on Preventing Soul-Beast Extinction&quot;</li></ol><h2 id="vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" tabindex="-1">VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Supervision plan self-consistency: high</strong>. The network operating principle is law-precedently defined</li><li><strong>Retcon-ending risk: near zero</strong></li><li><strong>Comparison</strong>: Dou relies on &quot;spirit soul&quot; patches to temporarily prolong life; the supervision plan prevents it from the root</li></ul><p>The supervision web&#39;s value lies in turning &quot;protect soul beasts&quot; from a conscience problem into an engineering problem. Population data real-time public, red-line species auto-warned, however strong a genius cannot kill within the red line. A civilization that pins hope on strong ones&#39; kindness will eventually lose to a civilization that writes hope into institutions.</p><p>The Alaya supervision web must also be paired with an &quot;appeal and dynamic adjustment&quot; mechanism: population data fluctuates; thresholds need to be loosened as ecology recovers. It is not an unchanging ban, but a learning ecological management system. Lin-Hao-style reconstructors designing it both prevent humans over-hunting and prevent the supervision itself from rigidifying — good institutions must both manage predation and leave room for symbiotic growth.</p><p>The Alaya supervision web must also solve the problem of &quot;who supervises the supervisors.&quot; If the supervision web itself is manipulated by strong ones, it becomes a new oppressive tool. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s design is: supervision data public whole-network, thresholds legislated by the council, changes adjudicated by the symbiotic court. Lin-Hao-style reconstructors put supervisory power into the institutional cage, rather than handing it to some new strong one. Good supervision both prevents humans over-hunting and prevents supervisors abusing power — this is the dual goal of institutional design.</p><p>Supplementary verdict: the supervision web must also solve &quot;who supervises the supervisors.&quot; Data public whole-network, thresholds legislated, changes adjudicated by court; supervisory power itself is also put in the cage. Good supervision both prevents humans over-hunting and prevents supervisors abusing power — Lin-Hao-style reconstructors design for both risks from the start.</p><p>Good supervision both prevents over-hunting and prevents power abuse. Only when both risks are caught together does the institution not change from a cage into a new shackle.</p><p>Supervision&#39;s measure lies precisely in both daring to manage and leaving room for growth.</p><p>Supervision&#39;s maturity mark is that it neither makes people feel oppressed, nor leaves loopholes to exploit. The Alaya web and Path D — one guards, one nourishes; the former blocks today&#39;s over-hunting, the latter cancels tomorrow&#39;s demand; the two-pronged approach is the complete solution.</p><p><strong>Old-new cosmos resource comparison</strong>: old-cosmos resources and Great Dao are finite, inevitably predatory involution; Anchor Symbiosis has everyone inherently possessing infinite origin, predation loses meaning.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: irreversible extinction is stopped in advance</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: the red-line system cages &quot;the other as resource&quot;</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang Luo had no supervision consciousness at all; Dou at least needs to make up this lesson</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: soul-beast populations receive institutional protection for the first time</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: the supervision web can be exported to any plane with companion species</li><li><strong>Universal equal infinite law</strong>: basic infinite power is inherent in all; the easygoing retain a guarantee, strivers can superimpose higher; infinite origin erases predatory motivation, predatory involution loses meaning from the root</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Soul beasts should not live by the protagonist&#39;s pity, but by institutional protection. What the Alaya supervision web must do is make &quot;hunted to extinction&quot; institutionally impossible in the Dou world.</p><p>In the final analysis, Dou Continent · Alaya supervision plan · institutional design to prevent soul-beast extinction described in this document is no isolated case — its causality and energy-level traces are filed throughout in the Alaya Network, traceable and verifiable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./365_模块2-斗罗-魂兽灭绝危机-掠夺式修炼的生态灾难.html">Entry 365 · Soul-Beast Extinction Crisis</a> · <a href="./385_模块2-斗罗-万族共和方案-打破人族本位与武魂歧视.html">Entry 385 · Myriad-Ranks Republican Plan</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/21-共生网络运作原理.html">21-Symbiotic-Network Operating Principle</a></li><li>Official site: <a href="https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/</a></li></ul>',33)])])}const g=t(s,[["render",a]]);export{c as __pageData,g as default};
